Till you want some more</i>


00:00:39.721 --> 00:00:43.452
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:47.425
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:47.595 --> 00:00:51.190
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:54.927
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:55.103 --> 00:00:58.630
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:58.807 --> 00:01:02.174
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:01:02.344 --> 00:01:05.609
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.477
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:09.651 --> 00:01:13.678
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:13.855 --> 00:01:17.450
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:20.753
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:24.695
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:27.858
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:28.036 --> 00:01:31.528
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:31.706 --> 00:01:34.971
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:35.143 --> 00:01:37.168
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:38.613 --> 00:01:41.446
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:46.514
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:49.987
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:50.158 --> 00:01:52.092
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:27.195 --> 00:02:30.756
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:30.932 --> 00:02:32.092
You have an appointment...


00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.861
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:35.036 --> 00:02:37.971
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:38.139 --> 00:02:40.198
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:41.899
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:42.343 --> 00:02:44.174
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:44.345 --> 00:02:46.176
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:46.614 --> 00:02:47.740
Bath. Now.


00:02:48.716 --> 00:02:50.581
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:53.181
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:56.758 --> 00:02:58.851
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:01.621
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:03:01.796 --> 00:03:04.230
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:17.712 --> 00:03:19.145
Victor, no.


00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:27.754
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:27.922 --> 00:03:33.918
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:34.395 --> 00:03:36.920
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:37.632 --> 00:03:39.327
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:40.835 --> 00:03:42.427
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:42.971 --> 00:03:44.336
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:45.507 --> 00:03:47.134
Nothing.


00:03:51.779 --> 00:03:54.646
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:54.816 --> 00:03:56.181
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:02.013
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:05.421
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:04:05.593 --> 00:04:09.051
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.324
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.161
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:14.335 --> 00:04:16.530
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:16.704 --> 00:04:20.162
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:21.843 --> 00:04:24.107
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:24.279 --> 00:04:26.975
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:27.148 --> 00:04:30.242
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:30.418 --> 00:04:31.908
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:32.086 --> 00:04:34.646
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:34.822 --> 00:04:36.619
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:50.171 --> 00:04:54.130
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:54.309 --> 00:04:57.676
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:57.845 --> 00:04:59.710
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:04:59.881 --> 00:05:02.315
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:05:02.483 --> 00:05:06.010
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:05:06.187 --> 00:05:09.748
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:10.258 --> 00:05:15.161
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.161
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:17.665 --> 00:05:21.658
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:27.471
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:27.942 --> 00:05:33.005
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:33.314 --> 00:05:36.442
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:36.618 --> 00:05:39.678
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:41.356 --> 00:05:43.620
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:43.791 --> 00:05:47.227
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.724
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:51.899 --> 00:05:53.730
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:55.003 --> 00:05:58.200
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:58.373 --> 00:06:02.139
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.971
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:06:05.146 --> 00:06:06.909
That record was amazing.


00:06:07.081 --> 00:06:10.050
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:11.552 --> 00:06:14.020
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:14.188 --> 00:06:17.089
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:17.258 --> 00:06:18.919
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:20.461 --> 00:06:26.024
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.361
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:28.536 --> 00:06:31.903
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:32.073 --> 00:06:34.234
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:34.409 --> 00:06:36.775
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:36.944 --> 00:06:40.846
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:41.983 --> 00:06:44.076
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:44.585 --> 00:06:46.951
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:47.522 --> 00:06:49.649
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:49.824 --> 00:06:51.792
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:51.959 --> 00:06:53.950
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:54.128 --> 00:06:57.097
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:57.532 --> 00:07:00.296
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:07:00.468 --> 00:07:03.369
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:07:03.538 --> 00:07:05.369
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.407
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:08.576 --> 00:07:11.204
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.670
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:13.848 --> 00:07:15.440
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:15.616 --> 00:07:17.982
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:18.152 --> 00:07:21.553
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:22.156 --> 00:07:27.560
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:36.437 --> 00:07:38.132
Watch out.


00:07:38.606 --> 00:07:40.631
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:41.642 --> 00:07:45.237
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:45.413 --> 00:07:47.210
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:47.381 --> 00:07:49.747
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:49.917 --> 00:07:51.282
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:51.452 --> 00:07:54.444
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:54.622 --> 00:07:58.581
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.489
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:08:01.329 --> 00:08:03.229
You giving our ball back or what?


00:08:03.397 --> 00:08:07.026
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:11.839 --> 00:08:15.104
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:17.445 --> 00:08:21.176
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:21.349 --> 00:08:22.714
Hotter.


00:08:22.884 --> 00:08:24.511
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:24.685 --> 00:08:26.915
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:27.088 --> 00:08:29.648
First time for everything, right?


00:08:36.798 --> 00:08:38.493
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:38.666 --> 00:08:39.894
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:40.368 --> 00:08:43.428
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:43.604 --> 00:08:45.799
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:45.973 --> 00:08:49.431
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.874
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:52.046 --> 00:08:55.413
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:55.683 --> 00:08:58.015
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:58.186 --> 00:08:59.710
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:08:59.887 --> 00:09:02.788
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:09:02.957 --> 00:09:06.393
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:06.561 --> 00:09:10.088
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:10.264 --> 00:09:15.429
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:15.603 --> 00:09:19.164
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.433
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:21.609 --> 00:09:24.510
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:24.679 --> 00:09:26.806
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:26.981 --> 00:09:30.007
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:30.184 --> 00:09:32.379
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:40.928 --> 00:09:42.190
Whoa.


00:09:42.363 --> 00:09:45.457
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:45.633 --> 00:09:48.295
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:48.469 --> 00:09:49.629
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:49.804 --> 00:09:53.205
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:53.374 --> 00:09:55.035
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:55.209 --> 00:09:56.233
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.878
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:59.046 --> 00:10:01.446
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:10:01.616 --> 00:10:03.516
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:10:03.684 --> 00:10:05.311
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:10:05.887 --> 00:10:07.980
Om.


00:10:08.789 --> 00:10:11.417
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:11.592 --> 00:10:13.685
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:13.861 --> 00:10:16.386
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:16.764 --> 00:10:18.391
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:19.901 --> 00:10:21.061
My butt is numb.


00:10:21.402 --> 00:10:24.599
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:24.772 --> 00:10:28.230
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:28.409 --> 00:10:31.503
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:31.679 --> 00:10:33.670
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:34.749 --> 00:10:40.585
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:40.755 --> 00:10:44.316
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:45.192 --> 00:10:48.252
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:48.429 --> 00:10:51.023
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:51.198 --> 00:10:52.495
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:52.667 --> 00:10:55.192
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:55.369 --> 00:10:58.566
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:58.739 --> 00:11:01.173
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:11:01.342 --> 00:11:04.743
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:08.516 --> 00:11:09.983
Victor.


00:11:10.151 --> 00:11:15.384
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:39.046 --> 00:11:43.483
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:43.818 --> 00:11:46.309
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:47.355 --> 00:11:50.017
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:50.191 --> 00:11:54.753
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:58.065 --> 00:11:59.089
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:59.266 --> 00:12:01.700
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:12:01.869 --> 00:12:03.461
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:12:03.671 --> 00:12:05.901
Mac and cheese.


00:12:06.807 --> 00:12:09.935
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:10.478 --> 00:12:12.036
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:17.551 --> 00:12:20.918
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:21.088 --> 00:12:24.421
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:25.826 --> 00:12:29.023
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:29.196 --> 00:12:31.289
How did this become my life?


00:12:31.465 --> 00:12:34.457
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:34.635 --> 00:12:36.125
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:36.303 --> 00:12:37.736
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:38.172 --> 00:12:40.367
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:40.541 --> 00:12:42.873
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:45.713 --> 00:12:48.580
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:50.351 --> 00:12:51.648
Now look at me.


00:12:51.819 --> 00:12:54.310
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:54.488 --> 00:12:57.480
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:57.658 --> 00:12:59.649
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:12:59.827 --> 00:13:02.057
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:02.229 --> 00:13:03.992
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:05.533 --> 00:13:07.728
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:07.902 --> 00:13:10.393
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:10.805 --> 00:13:14.036
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:14.208 --> 00:13:17.974
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:18.145 --> 00:13:21.774
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:22.716 --> 00:13:25.116
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:25.286 --> 00:13:27.880
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:28.055 --> 00:13:30.922
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:31.092 --> 00:13:32.116
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:32.293 --> 00:13:34.853
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:35.029 --> 00:13:36.963
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:37.131 --> 00:13:40.157
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:40.334 --> 00:13:42.359
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:42.536 --> 00:13:44.504
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:44.672 --> 00:13:45.696
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:45.873 --> 00:13:49.741
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:53.311
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:53.481 --> 00:13:56.575
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.048
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:01.154
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:01.322 --> 00:14:03.552
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:03.724 --> 00:14:06.921
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:07.094 --> 00:14:11.360
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:11.532 --> 00:14:13.500
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:14.001 --> 00:14:17.528
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:20.074 --> 00:14:25.512
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:25.679 --> 00:14:28.239
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:28.415 --> 00:14:30.508
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:30.684 --> 00:14:32.413
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:32.586 --> 00:14:35.214
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:35.389 --> 00:14:38.722
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:38.893 --> 00:14:40.520
Again.


00:14:40.694 --> 00:14:42.252
Really? Okay.


00:14:42.429 --> 00:14:48.061
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:48.235 --> 00:14:49.361
Ouch.


00:14:49.537 --> 00:14:52.597
I could belch the song better.


00:14:54.208 --> 00:14:56.369
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:56.544 --> 00:14:58.011
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:58.179 --> 00:15:01.080
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:01.248 --> 00:15:05.150
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:05.519 --> 00:15:09.182
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:13.394 --> 00:15:15.760
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.659
No.


00:15:17.831 --> 00:15:20.129
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:32.313 --> 00:15:35.612
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:35.783 --> 00:15:38.251
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:48.729 --> 00:15:51.823
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:56.704 --> 00:15:58.433
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:58.606 --> 00:15:59.698
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:59.873 --> 00:16:03.969
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:04.144 --> 00:16:05.475
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:05.646 --> 00:16:08.410
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:08.849 --> 00:16:10.146
Victor!


00:16:10.317 --> 00:16:13.548
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:13.721 --> 00:16:15.882
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:19.393 --> 00:16:21.020
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:30.938 --> 00:16:32.098
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:32.273 --> 00:16:33.672
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:33.841 --> 00:16:37.277
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:37.444 --> 00:16:39.105
Crap.


00:16:42.516 --> 00:16:44.211
This is insane.


00:16:44.385 --> 00:16:48.446
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:58.232 --> 00:17:00.325
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:02.069 --> 00:17:03.696
Crap.


00:17:07.007 --> 00:17:10.602
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:10.778 --> 00:17:14.578
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:14.748 --> 00:17:16.875
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:17.051 --> 00:17:18.746
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:18.919 --> 00:17:21.479
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:21.655 --> 00:17:24.715
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:24.892 --> 00:17:27.122
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:27.294 --> 00:17:29.421
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:31.765 --> 00:17:33.232
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:39.406 --> 00:17:41.271
Victor.


00:17:45.112 --> 00:17:46.545
Katie?


00:17:47.748 --> 00:17:49.978
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:50.184 --> 00:17:53.449
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.384
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:57.424 --> 00:17:59.255
The truth. Um...


00:18:00.561 --> 00:18:03.894
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:04.064 --> 00:18:05.395
Naked.


00:18:06.433 --> 00:18:08.731
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:08.902 --> 00:18:10.426
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:12.873 --> 00:18:13.965
There.


00:18:14.141 --> 00:18:17.338
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:21.949 --> 00:18:23.576
I'm kidding.


00:18:24.118 --> 00:18:25.949
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:26.286 --> 00:18:27.310
No, no.


00:18:27.488 --> 00:18:30.889
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:31.058 --> 00:18:33.253
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:33.861 --> 00:18:38.525
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:39.032 --> 00:18:42.832
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:43.003 --> 00:18:45.597
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:49.476 --> 00:18:51.137
What is that?


00:18:51.712 --> 00:18:53.976
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:54.148 --> 00:18:56.116
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:57.317 --> 00:18:59.046
Hey. What...?


00:19:11.899 --> 00:19:14.390
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:14.568 --> 00:19:16.195
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.497
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:18.672 --> 00:19:20.936
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:21.108 --> 00:19:22.132
Do you hear this?


00:19:22.309 --> 00:19:23.970
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:24.144 --> 00:19:25.839
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:26.013 --> 00:19:28.345
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:28.515 --> 00:19:30.710
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:30.884 --> 00:19:32.749
She gave you a CD?


00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:36.287
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:37.524 --> 00:19:41.392
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:42.629 --> 00:19:46.725
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:48.702 --> 00:19:50.897
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:52.039 --> 00:19:53.597
So...


00:19:54.475 --> 00:19:56.602
...that meeting today...


00:19:56.777 --> 00:19:59.575
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:59.913 --> 00:20:01.972
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:02.149 --> 00:20:04.583
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:04.852 --> 00:20:06.046
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:07.521 --> 00:20:09.421
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:12.718
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:12.993 --> 00:20:16.724
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:21.635 --> 00:20:24.433
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:24.605 --> 00:20:27.665
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:27.841 --> 00:20:30.105
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:34.081 --> 00:20:35.742
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:37.417 --> 00:20:38.714
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:38.886 --> 00:20:41.980
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:42.155 --> 00:20:44.623
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:44.791 --> 00:20:46.952
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:47.127 --> 00:20:48.321
That's interesting.


00:20:48.495 --> 00:20:51.259
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:51.431 --> 00:20:52.659
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:52.833 --> 00:20:54.460
I only have cheese.


00:20:57.638 --> 00:20:59.606
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:59.773 --> 00:21:01.673
Your phone.


00:21:04.711 --> 00:21:07.578
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:07.748 --> 00:21:09.306
I have underestimated you.


00:21:09.883 --> 00:21:11.714
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:11.885 --> 00:21:14.979
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:15.155 --> 00:21:17.783
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:17.958 --> 00:21:22.156
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:22.329 --> 00:21:25.594
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:25.766 --> 00:21:29.202
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:29.369 --> 00:21:32.497
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:32.673 --> 00:21:37.804
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:39.079 --> 00:21:41.240
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:46.653 --> 00:21:51.283
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:51.458 --> 00:21:55.554
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:55.729 --> 00:21:59.495
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:59.967 --> 00:22:01.628
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:01.802 --> 00:22:03.963
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:07.207 --> 00:22:09.903
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:10.477 --> 00:22:13.935
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:14.381 --> 00:22:16.349
I like trouble.


00:22:17.884 --> 00:22:19.010
Hey, kids.


00:22:20.320 --> 00:22:23.756
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:23.924 --> 00:22:26.688
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:30.694
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:30.998 --> 00:22:36.231
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:36.436 --> 00:22:38.904
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:39.172 --> 00:22:41.732
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:41.908 --> 00:22:43.876
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:44.044 --> 00:22:47.104
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:50.340
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:50.517 --> 00:22:53.213
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:53.387 --> 00:22:56.686
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:56.857 --> 00:22:58.688
What if I don't want to?


00:22:59.793 --> 00:23:03.524
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:03.697 --> 00:23:05.756
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:05.932 --> 00:23:08.196
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:08.368 --> 00:23:11.929
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:12.105 --> 00:23:13.595
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:13.774 --> 00:23:15.241
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:16.843 --> 00:23:18.970
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:19.146 --> 00:23:22.274
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:22.683 --> 00:23:26.881
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:27.054 --> 00:23:30.888
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:31.058 --> 00:23:33.959
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:34.127 --> 00:23:36.391
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:36.563 --> 00:23:38.690
You are a star.


00:23:38.865 --> 00:23:43.063
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:43.236 --> 00:23:44.794
I'm a star.


00:23:44.971 --> 00:23:49.135
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:49.309 --> 00:23:51.709
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:51.878 --> 00:23:53.846
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:54.014 --> 00:23:55.572
Every part of him.


00:23:55.749 --> 00:23:59.276
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:59.453 --> 00:24:02.217
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:03.490 --> 00:24:06.050
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:06.226 --> 00:24:08.126
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:08.729 --> 00:24:10.629
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:10.797 --> 00:24:13.493
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:13.667 --> 00:24:15.726
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:15.902 --> 00:24:17.267
Are we clear?


00:24:17.704 --> 00:24:18.898
Crystal.


00:24:20.841 --> 00:24:23.833
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:28.003
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:28.181 --> 00:24:30.649
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:30.817 --> 00:24:32.148
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:32.319 --> 00:24:34.446
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:34.621 --> 00:24:36.145
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:36.323 --> 00:24:39.690
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:39.860 --> 00:24:42.556
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:42.729 --> 00:24:44.993
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:45.165 --> 00:24:46.723
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:46.900 --> 00:24:49.027
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:49.202 --> 00:24:50.669
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:50.837 --> 00:24:53.670
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:56.502
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:56.676 --> 00:24:58.439
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:58.612 --> 00:25:00.307
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:00.747 --> 00:25:03.443
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:03.617 --> 00:25:06.347
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:07.714
We're here to impress.


00:25:07.888 --> 00:25:10.152
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:13.994 --> 00:25:16.462
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:16.630 --> 00:25:18.894
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:19.065 --> 00:25:21.260
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:21.434 --> 00:25:24.801
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:24.971 --> 00:25:27.496
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:27.674 --> 00:25:30.939
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:31.111 --> 00:25:36.413
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:36.583 --> 00:25:43.318
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:44.524 --> 00:25:46.014
That's good.


00:25:53.066 --> 00:25:56.365
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:57.204 --> 00:25:59.536
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:59.706 --> 00:26:01.606
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:02.642 --> 00:26:06.237
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:06.413 --> 00:26:08.608
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:08.782 --> 00:26:10.716
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:10.884 --> 00:26:16.117
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:16.289 --> 00:26:18.484
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:19.025 --> 00:26:20.788
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:20.961 --> 00:26:23.555
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:24.164 --> 00:26:27.463
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:27.634 --> 00:26:29.101
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:29.269 --> 00:26:31.294
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:31.471 --> 00:26:34.463
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:36.643 --> 00:26:39.077
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:42.616 --> 00:26:44.447
Okay.


00:26:45.018 --> 00:26:47.384
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:47.721 --> 00:26:49.484
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:49.656 --> 00:26:51.647
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:51.825 --> 00:26:53.656
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:53.827 --> 00:26:56.125
That I shall not cross.


00:26:56.596 --> 00:26:58.894
So sing something.


00:27:00.567 --> 00:27:02.034
Okay.


00:27:06.172 --> 00:27:08.970
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:09.142 --> 00:27:11.633
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:11.811 --> 00:27:13.210
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:13.680 --> 00:27:15.671
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:17.484 --> 00:27:19.952
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:20.120 --> 00:27:22.645
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:22.822 --> 00:27:24.414
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:24.925 --> 00:27:26.552
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:27.560 --> 00:27:30.495
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:30.664 --> 00:27:32.996
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:33.166 --> 00:27:34.633
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:36.036 --> 00:27:37.697
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:38.638 --> 00:27:41.471
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:41.641 --> 00:27:46.840
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:47.013 --> 00:27:48.571
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:49.683 --> 00:27:52.277
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:52.452 --> 00:27:55.012
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:55.188 --> 00:27:59.557
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:00.961 --> 00:28:03.623
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:03.797 --> 00:28:06.061
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:06.232 --> 00:28:08.894
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:09.069 --> 00:28:11.560
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:16.042 --> 00:28:18.169
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:18.345 --> 00:28:20.973
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:21.147 --> 00:28:24.480
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:24.751 --> 00:28:27.242
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:29.411
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:29.589 --> 00:28:31.887
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:32.058 --> 00:28:33.753
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:34.027 --> 00:28:35.722
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:36.162 --> 00:28:39.996
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:40.467 --> 00:28:44.563
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:44.738 --> 00:28:45.762
...good acoustics.


00:28:46.172 --> 00:28:50.006
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:50.176 --> 00:28:51.768
If you gave them your song.


00:28:53.179 --> 00:28:54.840
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:55.582 --> 00:28:58.278
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:58.451 --> 00:28:59.782
Yeah.


00:29:01.454 --> 00:29:07.984
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:08.294 --> 00:29:09.591
You wrote that song today?


00:29:09.763 --> 00:29:13.221
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:14.797
You really like this guy.


00:29:14.968 --> 00:29:16.663
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:16.836 --> 00:29:19.031
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:19.205 --> 00:29:22.697
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:24.511 --> 00:29:27.309
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:30.917 --> 00:29:33.750
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:35.789 --> 00:29:38.257
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:38.591 --> 00:29:42.083
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:42.262 --> 00:29:44.287
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:44.464 --> 00:29:45.488
Am not.


00:29:46.533 --> 00:29:49.525
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:49.702 --> 00:29:52.398
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:52.572 --> 00:29:55.132
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:55.308 --> 00:29:58.004
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:58.178 --> 00:30:00.112
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:00.280 --> 00:30:04.307
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:04.684 --> 00:30:07.778
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:10.723 --> 00:30:12.247
Okay.


00:30:12.559 --> 00:30:14.151
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:14.327 --> 00:30:15.658
That's my girl.


00:30:15.929 --> 00:30:19.922
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:20.100 --> 00:30:23.399
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:23.570 --> 00:30:25.333
What? Why?


00:30:25.505 --> 00:30:26.870
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:30.777 --> 00:30:32.335
Katie!


00:30:32.512 --> 00:30:35.948
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:36.116 --> 00:30:37.606
Go.


00:30:37.784 --> 00:30:39.513
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:39.686 --> 00:30:41.017
Angie, heads up.


00:30:42.989 --> 00:30:44.286
Katie!


00:30:49.496 --> 00:30:51.225
What's going on?


00:30:51.397 --> 00:30:52.830
Nothing.


00:30:52.999 --> 00:30:56.127
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:56.302 --> 00:30:58.600
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:58.771 --> 00:31:02.832
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:06.079 --> 00:31:10.243
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:10.416 --> 00:31:12.646
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:12.819 --> 00:31:14.252
Oh, no, no.


00:31:14.420 --> 00:31:16.911
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:17.090 --> 00:31:19.388
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:19.559 --> 00:31:22.255
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:22.428 --> 00:31:23.452
Fun.


00:31:23.630 --> 00:31:26.758
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:26.933 --> 00:31:30.334
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:31.204 --> 00:31:33.229
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:37.210 --> 00:31:39.576
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:39.913 --> 00:31:42.177
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:42.482 --> 00:31:45.576
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:45.852 --> 00:31:49.015
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:49.355 --> 00:31:52.415
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:52.592 --> 00:31:54.992
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:55.161 --> 00:31:58.096
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:58.264 --> 00:32:02.291
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:02.569 --> 00:32:05.868
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:07.073 --> 00:32:08.370
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:18.351 --> 00:32:20.615
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:20.787 --> 00:32:22.982
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:23.590 --> 00:32:26.616
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:27.794 --> 00:32:30.922
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:31.698 --> 00:32:33.962
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:34.133 --> 00:32:36.431
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:36.603 --> 00:32:39.800
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:43.009 --> 00:32:45.637
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:45.812 --> 00:32:48.872
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:49.048 --> 00:32:52.245
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:53.152 --> 00:32:56.019
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:56.189 --> 00:32:58.248
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:58.424 --> 00:32:59.516
I'm talking to Luke.


00:33:00.126 --> 00:33:02.617
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:02.795 --> 00:33:04.262
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:04.998 --> 00:33:06.329
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:06.499 --> 00:33:07.523
Mm-hm.


00:33:07.700 --> 00:33:09.099
Right.


00:33:10.103 --> 00:33:11.502
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:14.574 --> 00:33:15.836
Hmm.


00:33:20.647 --> 00:33:22.638
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:23.316 --> 00:33:24.340
Ravi?


00:33:26.019 --> 00:33:28.544
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:28.721 --> 00:33:31.155
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:33.293 --> 00:33:35.853
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:36.029 --> 00:33:37.223
Obviously.


00:33:37.764 --> 00:33:40.255
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:40.433 --> 00:33:41.991
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:42.168 --> 00:33:45.535
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:46.072 --> 00:33:49.200
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:49.375 --> 00:33:52.037
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:52.412 --> 00:33:55.813
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:55.982 --> 00:33:57.847
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:58.217 --> 00:33:59.741
But I never got my shot.


00:33:59.919 --> 00:34:02.149
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:02.322 --> 00:34:04.722
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:04.891 --> 00:34:07.086
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:07.260 --> 00:34:08.750
"Who is asking?"


00:34:09.028 --> 00:34:12.395
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:12.565 --> 00:34:15.159
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:15.335 --> 00:34:19.704
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:20.006 --> 00:34:22.270
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:22.442 --> 00:34:24.842
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:25.178 --> 00:34:27.806
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:27.980 --> 00:34:29.174
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:30.383 --> 00:34:33.079
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:35.888 --> 00:34:39.551
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:40.226 --> 00:34:42.285
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:42.462 --> 00:34:44.930
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:45.098 --> 00:34:46.156
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:47.734 --> 00:34:49.065
Blow it up.


00:34:51.003 --> 00:34:52.561
Thank you.


00:35:02.382 --> 00:35:03.781
Whoa.


00:35:03.950 --> 00:35:06.578
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:06.753 --> 00:35:09.813
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:11.190 --> 00:35:13.522
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:13.693 --> 00:35:16.924
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:19.632 --> 00:35:22.601
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:22.769 --> 00:35:26.398
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:27.106 --> 00:35:29.438
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:34.814 --> 00:35:36.247
Where is he?


00:35:37.083 --> 00:35:39.881
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:40.052 --> 00:35:41.713
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:41.888 --> 00:35:44.322
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:47.827 --> 00:35:51.388
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:51.564 --> 00:35:54.897
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:55.067 --> 00:35:57.262
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:57.470 --> 00:36:00.200
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:00.373 --> 00:36:02.807
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:09.615 --> 00:36:10.673
I think I found him.


00:36:10.850 --> 00:36:13.114
Well, he is blond.


00:36:16.222 --> 00:36:18.520
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:20.426 --> 00:36:22.724
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:22.895 --> 00:36:24.294
What are you doing here?


00:36:24.464 --> 00:36:27.297
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:27.467 --> 00:36:29.492
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:29.669 --> 00:36:32.604
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:32.772 --> 00:36:34.603
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:34.774 --> 00:36:37.242
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:39.679 --> 00:36:41.806
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:43.349 --> 00:36:46.785
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:46.953 --> 00:36:49.148
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:49.322 --> 00:36:52.189
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:52.358 --> 00:36:54.292
...and you're fired.


00:36:57.330 --> 00:37:00.857
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:03.469 --> 00:37:04.959
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:05.204 --> 00:37:06.330
You were amazing.


00:37:06.506 --> 00:37:07.564
Do I know you?


00:37:11.911 --> 00:37:14.505
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:16.849 --> 00:37:18.908
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:19.552 --> 00:37:22.043
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:26.559 --> 00:37:29.392
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:29.562 --> 00:37:30.927
Miss Van R.


00:37:31.564 --> 00:37:33.964
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:34.133 --> 00:37:35.327
...but were never good enough?


00:37:36.702 --> 00:37:38.363
Who told you that?


00:37:56.088 --> 00:37:57.521
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:57.690 --> 00:38:00.887
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:01.060 --> 00:38:02.186
Oh!


00:38:02.361 --> 00:38:06.593
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:10.937 --> 00:38:14.031
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:14.206 --> 00:38:17.107
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:21.881 --> 00:38:24.611
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:24.951 --> 00:38:27.647
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:27.820 --> 00:38:29.082
Follow me.


00:38:34.126 --> 00:38:35.957
Oh, wow.


00:38:38.431 --> 00:38:43.994
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:44.870 --> 00:38:46.770
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:46.939 --> 00:38:50.636
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:52.144 --> 00:38:53.338
Or not.


00:38:55.615 --> 00:38:58.641
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:04.857 --> 00:39:08.418
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:09.729 --> 00:39:13.961
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:14.133 --> 00:39:17.660
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:17.837 --> 00:39:21.830
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:23.809 --> 00:39:27.142
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:28.914 --> 00:39:32.611
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:33.285 --> 00:39:36.982
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:37.456 --> 00:39:40.289
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:40.760 --> 00:39:41.852
Uh-uh.


00:42:20.786 --> 00:42:23.380
I think I've blown something.


00:42:23.556 --> 00:42:26.616
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:29.228 --> 00:42:30.786
Move it, fatso.


00:42:32.531 --> 00:42:39.130
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:39.872 --> 00:42:43.501
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:56.055 --> 00:42:57.488
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:57.656 --> 00:42:59.681
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:59.859 --> 00:43:02.419
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:02.595 --> 00:43:04.563
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:07.032 --> 00:43:08.397
I'm so sorry.


00:43:09.101 --> 00:43:10.329
What...? You...?


00:43:11.036 --> 00:43:12.697
Hey. Wait.


00:43:12.872 --> 00:43:14.100
But who are you?


00:43:14.273 --> 00:43:16.867
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:25.017 --> 00:43:28.043
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:46.505 --> 00:43:48.530
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:49.308 --> 00:43:52.243
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:52.678 --> 00:43:55.613
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:55.948 --> 00:43:58.143
Don't talk about her like that.


00:44:00.152 --> 00:44:03.315
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:03.489 --> 00:44:07.050
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:07.226 --> 00:44:09.490
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:09.662 --> 00:44:12.722
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:13.032 --> 00:44:16.160
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:17.069 --> 00:44:20.197
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:26.712 --> 00:44:29.943
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:30.115 --> 00:44:32.174
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:32.351 --> 00:44:34.285
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:34.453 --> 00:44:36.148
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:36.322 --> 00:44:38.620
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:39.992 --> 00:44:44.122
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:45.097 --> 00:44:48.692
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:49.768 --> 00:44:51.395
We're recording.


00:44:51.704 --> 00:44:53.535
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:53.706 --> 00:44:54.934
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:55.541 --> 00:44:57.475
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:57.643 --> 00:44:59.372
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:59.545 --> 00:45:01.877
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:02.047 --> 00:45:03.275
Check this out, all right?


00:45:03.449 --> 00:45:07.044
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:07.219 --> 00:45:09.050
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:09.221 --> 00:45:11.052
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:11.256 --> 00:45:13.281
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:13.459 --> 00:45:14.619
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:14.793 --> 00:45:16.761
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:16.929 --> 00:45:18.794
That was subpar at best.


00:45:18.964 --> 00:45:21.489
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:22.234 --> 00:45:25.533
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:25.704 --> 00:45:27.262
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:27.439 --> 00:45:29.805
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:29.975 --> 00:45:33.001
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:33.178 --> 00:45:36.272
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:36.448 --> 00:45:38.006
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:38.450 --> 00:45:41.317
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:41.854 --> 00:45:45.415
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:45.691 --> 00:45:49.024
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:49.194 --> 00:45:51.788
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:51.964 --> 00:45:54.432
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:54.600 --> 00:45:57.694
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:57.870 --> 00:46:00.395
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:02.141 --> 00:46:06.737
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:06.912 --> 00:46:09.881
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:10.049 --> 00:46:12.882
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:18.924 --> 00:46:22.121
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:41.246 --> 00:46:43.544
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:43.715 --> 00:46:44.909
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:45.084 --> 00:46:47.382
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:47.553 --> 00:46:48.918
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:49.755 --> 00:46:51.882
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:52.057 --> 00:46:53.183
This is not good.


00:46:54.760 --> 00:46:56.557
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:56.728 --> 00:46:58.559
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:58.730 --> 00:47:01.130
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:01.300 --> 00:47:04.736
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:04.903 --> 00:47:05.927
Listen...


00:47:06.105 --> 00:47:09.541
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:09.708 --> 00:47:11.369
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:23.222 --> 00:47:27.215
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:27.392 --> 00:47:30.384
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:30.562 --> 00:47:34.191
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:34.366 --> 00:47:38.302
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:38.470 --> 00:47:42.270
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:42.808 --> 00:47:45.709
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:45.878 --> 00:47:48.938
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:50.749 --> 00:47:52.683
It was you?


00:47:53.352 --> 00:47:56.446
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:57.389 --> 00:48:01.223
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:02.861 --> 00:48:05.887
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:06.064 --> 00:48:08.828
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:09.001 --> 00:48:11.128
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:11.770 --> 00:48:14.500
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:14.773 --> 00:48:16.536
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:16.708 --> 00:48:20.075
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:20.245 --> 00:48:22.509
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:24.016 --> 00:48:25.813
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:25.984 --> 00:48:27.076
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:28.020 --> 00:48:29.487
You have a date with detention.


00:48:29.655 --> 00:48:31.122
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:31.290 --> 00:48:33.019
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:33.192 --> 00:48:35.888
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:36.061 --> 00:48:39.189
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:39.364 --> 00:48:40.854
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:41.033 --> 00:48:42.933
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:43.101 --> 00:48:45.899
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:46.071 --> 00:48:48.437
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:48.607 --> 00:48:50.074
Fine.


00:48:50.876 --> 00:48:52.400
I hate you.


00:48:56.048 --> 00:49:00.178
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:00.452 --> 00:49:02.386
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:08.961 --> 00:49:10.588
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:10.762 --> 00:49:13.959
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:14.132 --> 00:49:15.599
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:15.767 --> 00:49:18.565
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:18.737 --> 00:49:20.932
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


